  "notes": [
    "Each command has left and right variants. Unprefixed commands default to the right hand.",
    "Alternative packet: {\"command\":\"ui.click\",\"hand\":\"left\"}. Conflicting hand selectors are rejected.",
    "Left/right hand is separate from left/right mouse click: left.ui.rightclick means the left hand performs a right-click.",
    "Placement, movement, adjustment and menus belong to a hand. A screen being adjusted, moved or browsed by one hand cannot be acquired by the other.",
    "Shared commands affect the app or shared screen collection regardless of the issuing hand.",
    "Marker IDs determine left/right identity permanently. Normal centre fallback waits through brief marker tracking gaps; missing markers never borrow the other hand ray.",
    "hand.calibrate is retained as a compatibility status check for the selected root marker. Change marker IDs in the Unity Inspector to change the physical setup.",
    "Use a fresh id per action. Retry with the same id and socket; commands are deduplicated.",
    "appGestures override free-mode gestures only while pointing at the open app face. Timer digits: 10 min / 1 min / 10 sec / 1 sec; the timer and flashcard faces have no buttons. Settings, move, place and menus keep their existing controls. Explicit commands are never remapped.",
    "Twelve gestures: aliases swipt_left/swipt_right and wriggle_fingers are accepted. Legacy zoom_in/out still work but are not shown in the gesture panel.",
    "Click selects the swipe-highlighted menu item or aimed control, or performs the pointed app's primary action. Grab creates a screen on a valid blank surface, confirms an edit/move or accepts a menu choice; it does not operate an app. Wiggle toggles the pointed screen's settings (Choose app is the first option). Point-and-rotate turns a web browser or PDF screen vertical, or back to horizontal.",
    "Crumple cancels an edit or marks a pointed screen red for deletion. Grab confirms deletion only while pointing at that same red screen. Another gesture cancels the mark. Deletion never uses target memory.",
    "Resize and rotate lock the selected screen for that hand. Grab keeps changes; crumple restores the original size and rotation. Move keeps the old anchor until confirmed. Starting a move confirms earlier size/rotation edits.",
    "Timer left/right switches its look and screen shape (Blocks, Orbit, Capsule, Tower); up/down changes the digit the hand points towards, using the nearest digit in gaps and margins. Click starts/pauses, and resets a finished timer. Library up swipes scroll forward; down scrolls backward.",
    "Slider puzzle (3x3, 4x4, 5x5): click starts, pauses and resumes. While playing, a swipe slides the tile beside the gap in that direction. While ready, paused or solved, up/down make the board larger/smaller and left deals a new game; app.reset does the same from a remote sender.",
    "Hide the debug HUD to reveal the right-edge gesture guide strip. Point at it to open the guide; point away to dismiss. Works in normal and stereo goggle mode."
  ],
